        "content": "\nDrives \"most specific rule wins\" — a bug here silently misapplies survivorship rules in production data.\n\n```ts\n// types/rules.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ruleSpecificity } from \"@/types/rules\";\nimport type { SurvivorshipRule } from \"@/types/rules\";\n\nconst rule = (field: string, entityType: string): SurvivorshipRule => ({\n  id: \"r1\", field, entityType, strategy: \"escalate\", description: \"\",\n});\n\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  it(\"scores wildcard/wildcard lowest\", () => expect(ruleSpecificity(rule(\"*\", \"*\"))).toBe(0));\n  it(\"scores field-specific over wildcard field\", () => expect(ruleSpecificity(rule(\"name\", \"*\"))).toBe(2));\n  it(\"scores entityType-specific over wildcard entityType\", () => expect(ruleSpecificity(rule(\"*\", \"account\"))).toBe(1));\n  it(\"scores fully specific highest\", () => expect(ruleSpecificity(rule(\"name\", \"account\"))).toBe(3));\n  it(\"orders a specific rule ahead of a wildcard when sorted descending\", () => {\n    const rules = [rule(\"*\", \"*\"), rule(\"name\", \"account\")];\n    const sorted = [...rules].sort((a, b) => ruleSpecificity(b) - ruleSpecificity(a));\n    expect(sorted[0]).toBe(rules[1]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Missing integration test:** nothing exercises the actual \"first match wins, most specific first\" rule-evaluation *pipeline* — only the scoring function exists. There's no `applySurvivorship(rules, conflict)`-style function yet; when one is added, it needs a test for: no rule matches → escalate; two equally-specific rules → author order wins (documented behavior, currently unverified by any test).\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "4. Zod schemas (`types/*.ts`) — **entirely untested**",
        "content": "\nThese are the wire contract with the Python engine (`engine/pipeline/schema.py`) — the comment says \"mirrors X, change both in the same commit,\" which is exactly the kind of contract that needs a test to catch drift.\n\n**Gaps:** valid/invalid parse for each schema, refinement logic in `survivorshipRuleSchema` (the `prefer_source` requires `preferredSourceId` rule), discriminated union in `reviewActionSchema`.\n\n```ts\n// types/rules.test.ts (add to same file or a schema-specific file)\nimport { survivorshipRuleSchema, ruleStrategySchema } from \"@/types/rules\";\n\ndescribe(\"survivorshipRuleSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects prefer_source without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\", description: \"x\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts prefer_source with preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\",\n      preferredSourceId: \"src_1\", description: \"x\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts most_recent without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"most_recent\", description: \"x\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// types/resolution.test.ts\nimport { reviewActionSchema } from \"@/types/resolution\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewActionSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts approve with no extra fields\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"approve\" }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects override without overrideValue\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects override with empty-string overrideValue\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\", overrideValue: \"\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an unknown action\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"delete\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects a client-supplied reviewedBy (must not exist on the schema)\", () => {\n    const parsed = reviewActionSchema.parse({ action: \"approve\", reviewedBy: \"attacker\" });\n    expect(parsed).not.toHaveProperty(\"reviewedBy\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// types/source.test.ts\nimport { sourceConfigSchema, createSourceSchema } from \"@/types/source\";\n\ndescribe(\"sourceConfigSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty objects array\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"allows filter to be omitted\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [\"account\"] }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createSourceSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects name over 80 chars\", () => {\n    const result = createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"a\".repeat(81), kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"account\"] },\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an unknown source kind\", () => {\n    const result = createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"x\", kind: \"oracle\", config: { objects: [\"account\"] },\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "5. `lib/server/auth.ts` — `requireReviewer()` / `getReviewer()` — **untested, security-critical, needs mocking**",
        "content": "\nThis is the function the whole audit trail depends on (\"`actor` can never be a string the client supplied\"). No test currently proves it throws when unauthenticated, or that it correctly delegates to `reviewerLabel`.\n\n**Gaps:** unauthenticated throws; authenticated-but-no-`currentUser()` case; label delegation; `getReviewer()` returns `null` vs delegates to `requireReviewer()`.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/auth.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\", () => ({\n  auth: vi.fn(),\n  currentUser: vi.fn(),\n}));\n\nimport { auth, currentUser } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\nimport { requireReviewer, getReviewer } from \"@/lib/server/auth\";\n\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.resetAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is false\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null } as any);\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/No authenticated reviewer/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is true but userId is missing (matcher/handler disagreement)\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: null } as any);\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns userId and derived label on success\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"uid_1\" } as any);\n    vi.mocked(currentUser).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: null } as any);\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"uid_1\", label: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to userId as label when currentUser() resolves null\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"uid_1\" } as any);\n    vi.mocked(currentUser).mockResolvedValue(null);\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"uid_1\", label: \"uid_1\" });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getReviewer\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.resetAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"returns null when unauthenticated (does not throw)\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false } as any);\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"delegates to requireReviewer when authenticated\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"uid_1\" } as any);\n    vi.mocked(currentUser).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\" } as any);\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"uid_1\", label: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "6. `lib/server/sources.ts` — `listSources()` / `countSourcesBySide()` — **untested, DB access + parse boundary**",
        "content": "\n`listSources` re-validates every DB row through `sourceSchema.parse` — that's a runtime assertion that a malformed row throws, currently unverified. `countSourcesBySide` has real branching logic (which kinds map to which side).\n\n**Gaps:** empty result, parse failure on a malformed row (should throw, not silently pass through), side-counting for every kind including `synthetic` (mapped to neither crm nor warehouse bucket — is that intentional? worth a comment/test), duplicate-kind counting.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/sources.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nconst selectMock = vi.fn();\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/db\", () => ({ getDb: () => ({ select: selectMock }) }));\nvi.mock(\"next/server\", () => ({ connection: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined) }));\n\nimport { listSources, countSourcesBySide } from \"@/lib/server/sources\";\n\nfunction chain(rows: unknown[]) {\n  return { from: () => ({ orderBy: () => Promise.resolve(rows)) };\n}\n\ndescribe(\"listSources\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.resetAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"returns an empty array when there are no rows\", async () => {\n    selectMock.mockReturnValue(chain([]));\n    await expect(listSources()).resolves.toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws if a row fails schema validation (e.g. bad kind)\", async () => {\n    selectMock.mockReturnValue(chain([{\n      id: \"not-a-uuid\", name: \"x\", kind: \"oracle\", config: { objects: [] }, createdAt: new Date(),\n    }]));\n    await expect(listSources()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"countSourcesBySide\", () => {\n  it(\"buckets salesforce/hubspot as crm, databricks/snowflake as warehouse, synthetic separately\", async () => {\n    selectMock.mockReturnValue(chain([\n      { id: crypto.randomUUID(), name: \"a\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n      { id: crypto.randomUUID(), name: \"b\", kind: \"hubspot\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n      { id: crypto.randomUUID(), name: \"c\", kind: \"databricks\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n      { id: crypto.randomUUID(), name: \"d\", kind: \"synthetic\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n    ]));\n    await expect(countSourcesBySide()).resolves.toEqual({ crm: 2, warehouse: 1, synthetic: 1 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns all zeros when there are no sources\", async () => {\n    selectMock.mockReturnValue(chain([]));\n    await expect(countSourcesBySide()).resolves.toEqual({ crm: 0, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 0 });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "7. `lib/db/index.ts` — `getDb()` — **untested error path**",
        "content": "\n**Gap:** missing `DATABASE_URL` should throw with an actionable message — currently unverified. Also the module-level caching behavior (`globalForDb`) is unverified: a second call should reuse, not reconnect.\n\n```ts\n// lib/db/index.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\ndescribe(\"getDb\", () => {\n  const ORIGINAL_ENV = process.env.DATABASE_URL;\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    vi.resetModules();\n    delete (globalThis as any).canonDb;\n    delete (globalThis as any).canonSql;\n  });\n  afterEach(() => { process.env.DATABASE_URL = ORIGINAL_ENV; });\n\n  it(\"throws an actionable error when DATABASE_URL is unset\", async () => {\n    delete process.env.DATABASE_URL;\n    const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n    expect(() => getDb()).toThrow(/DATABASE_URL is not set/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"reuses the cached connection across calls\", async () => {\n    process.env.DATABASE_URL = \"postgres://localhost/test\";\n    const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n    expect(getDb()).toBe(getDb());\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "8. `proxy.ts` (Clerk middleware) — **untested route-matching logic**",
        "content": "\n`isPublicRoute` and the `matcher` regex are the entire authorization boundary for an internal tool handling org data. No test proves `/`, `/sign-in`, `/sign-up` bypass auth while everything else (including `/api/*`) requires it.\n\n```ts\n// proxy.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { createRouteMatcher } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\n\n// Re-derive the matcher the same way proxy.ts does, or export isPublicRoute for direct testing.\nconst isPublicRoute = createRouteMatcher([\"/\", \"/sign-in(.*)\", \"/sign-up(.*)\"]);\n\ndescribe(\"isPublicRoute\", () => {\n  it.each([\n    [\"/\", true],\n    [\"/sign-in\", true],\n    [\"/sign-in/factor-one\", true],\n    [\"/sign-up\", true],\n    [\"/sources\", false],\n    [\"/api/sources\", false],\n    [\"/sign-in-not-really\", true], // regex edge case worth confirming: does \"(.*)\" over-match a lookalike path?\n  ])(\"%s -> public=%s\", (path, expected) => {\n    const req = new Request(`https://example.com${path}`);\n    expect(isPublicRoute(req)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n});\n```\n`proxy.ts` doesn't export `isPublicRoute`, so this requires either exporting it or testing via an integration/E2E harness (Playwright hitting a dev server) — flag this as a **refactor-for-testability gap**.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "9. Components — **zero rendering tests**",
        "content": "\n- `SeverityMark` (`components/severity-mark.tsx`): pure mapping of `severity → mark/treatment/label`. Test that severity 1–4 each render the correct glyph count, treatment class, and — critically — **the label text is always present** (AGENTS.md constraint: \"never rendered without the word\").\n- `SourceTable`: renders empty `<tbody>` for `[]`, correct row count for N sources, joins `config.objects` correctly, handles a source with an empty `objects` array (blank cell, not a crash).\n- `SourcesEmptyState`: link hrefs (`/sources/new`, `/sources/new?kind=synthetic`) are present and correct — this is the actual product surface, worth a smoke test.\n\n```tsx\n// components/severity-mark.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SeverityMark } from \"@/components/severity-mark\";\n\ndescribe(\"SeverityMark\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4] as const)(\"renders the label for severity %d\", (severity) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={severity} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(/structural|attribute|cosmetic/i)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```tsx\n// components/sources/source-table.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SourceTable } from \"@/components/sources/source-table\";\n\nconst mkSource = (overrides = {}) => ({\n  id: crypto.randomUUID(), name: \"Prod SFDC\", kind: \"salesforce\" as const,\n  config: { objects: [\"Account\", \"Contact\"] }, createdAt: new Date(), ...overrides,\n});\n\ndescribe(\"SourceTable\", () => {\n  it(\"renders an empty tbody for no sources\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[]} />);\n    expect(screen.queryAllByRole(\"row\")).toHaveLength(1); // header only\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders one row per source with joined objects\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[mkSource()]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Account, Contact\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders a blank objects cell when config.objects is empty (should not crash)\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[mkSource({ config: { objects: [] } })]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Prod SFDC\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Integration test gaps (no coverage anywhere)",
        "content": "\nThere are no route handlers under `app/api/` yet in this snapshot, but the schemas (`reviewActionSchema`, `createSourceSchema`, `createRunSchema`) imply upcoming endpoints. Flag now, before they're built, so tests land with the code:\n\n1. **`PATCH /api/conflicts/:id/resolution`** (implied by `reviewActionSchema`) — end-to-end: authenticated request → `requireReviewer()` resolves actor → `audit_log` row written with server-derived `actor`, never client-supplied. This is the single highest-value integration test in the whole app given the explicit design constraint in `lib/server/auth.ts`'s docblock.\n2. **`SourcesPage` server component** — currently only manually verifiable; no test exercises the `sources.length === 0` branch (empty state) vs `> 0` branch (table + \"Add source\" button + count text), which is the actual UI logic in `app/(console)/sources/page.tsx:16-24`.\n3. **Ruleset evaluation pipeline** — `ruleSpecificity` exists but there's no `applySurvivorship`/`resolveConflict` function yet to integration-test end-to-end (rules → conflict → resolution). Worth a test the moment that function is written, given \"first match wins\" and \"no rule matches → escalate\" are both unverified behavioral guarantees today.\n4. **Table-ownership boundary** (`lib/db/schema.ts` comments: engine-only vs web-only tables) — no test currently prevents `lib/server/*.ts` from writing to `entities`/`matches`/`conflicts`. Worth either a lint rule or a smoke test once write paths exist.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Summary",
        "content": "| Area | Files | Status | Priority |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Pure utils | `cn.ts`, `reviewer-label.ts`, `rules.ts::ruleSpecificity` | 0% | High — cheap, no mocking |\n| Zod contracts | `types/*.ts` | 0% | High — engine/web drift risk |\n| Auth | `lib/server/auth.ts`, `proxy.ts` | 0% | Highest — security/audit-critical |\n| DB access | `lib/server/sources.ts`, `lib/db/index.ts` | 0% | Medium — needs mocking |\n| Components | `severity-mark.tsx`, `source-table.tsx`, `sources-empty-state.tsx` | 0% | Medium |\n| Route handlers / integration | none exist yet | N/A | Plan tests alongside implementation |\n\nRecommend starting with #1–#4 (pure functions + schemas) since they need zero mocking and cover the exact \"mirrors the Python engine\" and \"audit actor can't be client-supplied\" invariants the code comments call out as load-bearing.",
        "level": 3
      }
    ],
